WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.067
Former President Trump is

00:00:01.067 --> 00:00:02.869
continuing his attacks

00:00:02.869 --> 00:00:04.771
excuse me on his potential 2024

00:00:04.771 --> 00:00:05.772
Republican rival,

00:00:05.772 --> 00:00:06.539
and that is Florida

00:00:06.539 --> 00:00:08.241
Governor Ron DeSantis.

00:00:08.241 --> 00:00:09.843
Seniors Daniel Dale Fact-Check

00:00:09.843 --> 00:00:12.278
some of Trump's claims about DeSantis.

00:00:12.312 --> 00:00:12.879
So, Daniel,

00:00:12.879 --> 00:00:14.047
let's start with his claim

00:00:14.047 --> 00:00:15.949
that Florida is the third worst

00:00:15.949 --> 00:00:17.417
in crime in the country.

00:00:17.417 --> 00:00:19.519
Is that, in fact, true?

00:00:20.153 --> 00:00:21.354
Well, there's a handy trick

00:00:21.354 --> 00:00:23.189
for trying to make the country's

00:00:23.189 --> 00:00:25.091
most populous cities and states

00:00:25.091 --> 00:00:26.826
look like they're really bad on crime.

00:00:26.826 --> 00:00:27.994
And that is simply using

00:00:27.994 --> 00:00:29.529
their absolute totals

00:00:29.529 --> 00:00:31.531
without factoring in their population.

00:00:31.531 --> 00:00:33.199
So it is true that Florida has,

00:00:33.199 --> 00:00:33.867
as former

00:00:33.867 --> 00:00:34.968
President Trump said,

00:00:34.968 --> 00:00:35.969
the third most reported

00:00:35.969 --> 00:00:37.837
murders, rapes and aggravated assault.

00:00:37.837 --> 00:00:38.671
What he didn't mention

00:00:38.671 --> 00:00:39.572
is that that is largely

00:00:39.572 --> 00:00:41.674
because Florida has the third largest,

00:00:42.208 --> 00:00:43.576
most populous state.

00:00:43.576 --> 00:00:45.512
And so if you look at per capita figures,

00:00:45.512 --> 00:00:47.080
which is by far

00:00:47.080 --> 00:00:48.148
the fairer way

00:00:48.148 --> 00:00:49.849
to actually compare between states

00:00:49.849 --> 00:00:51.785
Florida fares notably better it's

00:00:51.785 --> 00:00:53.186
25th worst on murder.

00:00:53.186 --> 00:00:53.987
So right in the middle

00:00:53.987 --> 00:00:55.922
33rd worst unreported rape

00:00:55.922 --> 00:00:57.257
so better than the middle

00:00:57.257 --> 00:00:58.191
and 23rd

00:00:58.191 --> 00:01:00.260
worst on aggravated assault again

00:01:00.260 --> 00:01:01.127
right around the middle.

00:01:01.127 --> 00:01:02.595
So very important context

00:01:02.595 --> 00:01:03.563
that the former president

00:01:03.563 --> 00:01:04.497
is not mentioning here

00:01:06.166 --> 00:01:06.766
Daniel something

00:01:06.766 --> 00:01:07.767
fascinating about the former

00:01:07.767 --> 00:01:09.803
president is his ability

00:01:09.803 --> 00:01:13.106
to meld recollections of things

00:01:13.106 --> 00:01:13.673
like stories

00:01:13.673 --> 00:01:15.809
change as he tells them more and more

00:01:15.809 --> 00:01:16.242
and there's one

00:01:16.242 --> 00:01:18.344
that he keeps telling about

00:01:18.344 --> 00:01:21.114
yeah about how he only endorsed DeSantis

00:01:21.114 --> 00:01:22.082
for governor

00:01:22.082 --> 00:01:23.349
because he saw DeSantis

00:01:23.349 --> 00:01:24.050
defend him

00:01:24.050 --> 00:01:26.252
over his first impeachment battle.

00:01:27.287 --> 00:01:29.556
Set the record straight on that one.

00:01:29.722 --> 00:01:31.091
This is an easy fact check.

00:01:31.091 --> 00:01:32.192
And the fact is, is

00:01:32.192 --> 00:01:34.060
this could not possibly be true

00:01:34.060 --> 00:01:36.596
because the president's endorsement

00:01:36.596 --> 00:01:37.097
of then

00:01:37.097 --> 00:01:38.331
Congressman DeSantis

00:01:38.331 --> 00:01:41.101
for Florida governor came in mid 2018.

00:01:41.334 --> 00:01:41.868
The Trump

00:01:41.868 --> 00:01:42.735
first impeachment

00:01:42.735 --> 00:01:45.071
battle began in late 2019

00:01:45.071 --> 00:01:46.372
so he could not possibly

00:01:46.372 --> 00:01:47.707
have seen him on TV

00:01:47.707 --> 00:01:48.875
defending him on impeachment

00:01:48.875 --> 00:01:50.243
and then said what the heck,

00:01:50.243 --> 00:01:51.845
I'll endorse him for that reason.

00:01:51.845 --> 00:01:52.779
Now it is possible

00:01:52.779 --> 00:01:54.114
that Trump is thinking of DeSantis

00:01:54.114 --> 00:01:55.482
defending him on the Mueller

00:01:55.482 --> 00:01:57.517
Russia probe in 2017

00:01:57.517 --> 00:01:58.451
but Trump is the one

00:01:58.451 --> 00:02:00.120
who keeps raising Biden gaffes

00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:01.020
as if

00:02:01.087 --> 00:02:02.689
they're a sign of serious mental decline

00:02:02.689 --> 00:02:03.523
or something like that.

00:02:03.523 --> 00:02:04.891
So I think it's important to point out

00:02:04.891 --> 00:02:06.993
when Trump's own stories are

00:02:07.093 --> 00:02:08.761
similarly inaccurate.

00:02:08.761 --> 00:02:09.362
Well, to be fair,

00:02:09.362 --> 00:02:10.797
there have been several probes,

00:02:10.797 --> 00:02:11.865
so one can understand

00:02:11.865 --> 00:02:12.932
how you may confuse them

00:02:12.932 --> 00:02:14.801
in what year they happen in.

00:02:14.801 --> 00:02:15.435
Daniel Trump

00:02:15.435 --> 00:02:16.369
also has been attacking

00:02:16.369 --> 00:02:18.538
DeSantis over his pandemic policies.

00:02:18.771 --> 00:02:19.973
And in a statement last week,

00:02:19.973 --> 00:02:20.540
Trump claimed

00:02:20.540 --> 00:02:21.107
that DeSantis

00:02:21.107 --> 00:02:23.910
sealed all beaches and other places

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:26.279
for ended for extended periods of time.

00:02:26.312 --> 00:02:27.180
Is that one correct?

00:02:28.481 --> 00:02:29.782
This is an exaggeration.

00:02:29.782 --> 00:02:31.050
So it is true that Governor

00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:33.153
DeSantis closed some beaches in Florida.

00:02:33.153 --> 00:02:34.921
He didn't close all of them in March.

00:02:34.921 --> 00:02:35.588
20, 20.

00:02:35.588 --> 00:02:37.957
He ordered the closures of public beaches

00:02:38.057 --> 00:02:39.859
in Broward and Palm Beach counties, too

00:02:39.859 --> 00:02:40.860
populous counties.

00:02:40.860 --> 00:02:42.162
But he would not order

00:02:42.162 --> 00:02:43.029
a statewide closure.

00:02:43.029 --> 00:02:43.563
In fact,

00:02:43.563 --> 00:02:45.265
he was sued unsuccessfully

00:02:45.265 --> 00:02:47.300
for refusing to do a statewide closure

00:02:47.300 --> 00:02:48.568
on the other beaches.

00:02:48.568 --> 00:02:50.103
He simply order that people

00:02:50.103 --> 00:02:51.004
limit their gatherings

00:02:51.004 --> 00:02:52.338
to no more than ten people

00:02:52.338 --> 00:02:53.873
and stay six feet apart.

00:02:53.873 --> 00:02:56.176
And we know that was in line with what

00:02:56.309 --> 00:02:57.243
then President Trump

00:02:57.243 --> 00:02:58.611
and the Trump administration

00:02:58.611 --> 00:03:00.680
were urging people to do at the time.

00:03:00.713 --> 00:03:01.614
So the DeSantis

00:03:01.614 --> 00:03:02.282
order certainly did

00:03:02.282 --> 00:03:03.983
not come out of nowhere.

00:03:04.250 --> 00:03:06.152
All right, Daniel Dale, keeping us honest

00:03:06.152 --> 00:03:07.554
by always, fact checking everything.

00:03:07.554 --> 00:03:08.488
Thank you so much.

